## Capabilities

### graph — Knowledge Graph
100K+ thoughts, 6000+ sources, full-text search. Primary tool for orienting
around any topic. Scoped to the **{{ config.graph_project }}** org.

```bash
graph search "query"                  # FTS search (--or for ANY term)
graph search "query" --project {{ config.graph_project }}   # explicit org scope
graph attention --last 20             # human focus trail
graph read <src_id|tmux_name> --max-chars 3000  # read a full source
graph context <src_id|tmux_name> <turn>         # turns around a search hit
graph context <src_id|tmux_name> last           # latest turns of a source
graph tail <src_id|tmux_name> 20                # last N turns of a session
graph sessions --all                  # ingest latest session data before searching
graph sessions --status               # live session table (SOURCE column gives the id)
graph note "text" --tags tag          # persist an insight or pitfall for future agents
graph notes --since 1h                # recent notes by time
graph bead "title" --source <id>      # create a bead with provenance
graph primer <bead-id>                # full context primer: description + pitfalls + provenance
graph dispatch approve <bead-id>      # approve bead(s) for dispatch (accepts multiple IDs)
graph dispatch runs                   # running/queued agent activity
graph dispatch status                 # compact one-liner
graph wait <bead-id>                  # block until dispatched bead completes
graph crosstalk --since 1h            # recent CrossTalk messages
graph crosstalk send <s> "msg"        # send CrossTalk message (-c - for stdin)
graph crosstalk broadcast "msg"       # send to all live sessions
graph thought "text" --tags tag       # capture a raw idea
graph thread create "title"           # create a thought thread
graph thread park/done/active <id>    # manage thread lifecycle
graph collab topics                   # browse tag taxonomy with descriptions
graph set-label "title"               # set session working title
graph set-topics "Line 1" "Line 2"    # set card status lines
graph set-role researcher             # set session role
graph set-nag --interval 10           # enable idle nag (--off to disable)
graph share <file> --alt "..." --caption "..."  # render a file as an inline tile in the session viewer
```
Run `graph --help` for full reference.

**Reading a session by tmux name.** `graph read`, `graph context`, and `graph tail` accept either a source-id prefix or the tmux name shown by `graph sessions --status` (e.g. `auto-0506-001257`, `host-0506-095207`). Names containing non-hex characters are auto-resolved through the dashboard DB; pass them directly, no UUID lookup needed.

**Sharing files with the operator (`graph share`)**

Use `graph share <file> [--alt ...] [--caption ...]` to drop an image (or
any file) into the session viewer as an inline tile. One tool call →
one tile, rendered at the current turn. The operator clicks for fullscreen.

- **One share per Bash tool_result.** The harness up-converts a single JSON
  object whose `type` is `viewer_attachment`; chaining shares (`graph
  share a && graph share b`) in one Bash call concatenates two JSON
  objects and *neither* renders. Use one Bash invocation per share.
- **Don't print anything else in the same Bash call** — extra stdout
  breaks the parse.
- **No `--session` flag, no need.** The session is stamped from the
  trusted JSONL stream, not anything the agent prints.

Canonical how-to with examples + security model: `graph read 3570406f-29a`.

**Dispatch workflow:**
1. `graph dispatch approve <bead-id>` — release bead for dispatch
2. `graph wait <bead-id>` — block until dispatched bead completes
3. `graph dispatch status` — check overall queue at any time

